                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A fun little puzzle platformer.. though it can get frustrating at times ..sawmill i'm looking at you. \nCute/interesting art style. I have to say Eyas looks out of place.. it could be in the story.. no clue really.. i skipped it. The story is not what this game is about for me.. it's about hard platforming with interesting puzzles and mechanics , this game does that really well. The platforming feels good and is responsive, the puzzle make you think and it's not always immediately obvious what you need to do. This game is not easy, though not insanely hard. Some levels thankfully have checkpoint so that you don't need to do the entire level again. However the levels are very short but the checkpoint make it more enjoyable for me. There are also par times which you can try to beat, i did find these times ridiculously hard. I stopped trying after the first few levels, but it's there if you like that sort of thing. Some levels also have so called seer stones which you can collect. Music is good.. especially once you arrive in The Net world. \n\nIf you don't like figuring out what to do and dying a couple of times while doing that.. you are not gonna have a good time with this. If you do like a challenge in your puzzle platformer give this one a try.",
